##
#
# Isentropic vortex, Section 6.2 (i), Table 1 of [1].
#
# The isentropic vortex [2] is a smooth analytic solution of the
# compressible Euler equations with polytropic gas equation of state. The
# vortex has strength beta = 5, is initially centered at x_0 = (-1, -1),
# and is advected with velocity v_inf = (1, 1), i.e., with a speed of
# sqrt(2) in diagonal direction. At the final time t = 2 it is centered at
# (1, 1). The computational domain is [-5, 5]^2 with Dirichlet boundary
# conditions given by the exact solution, and gamma = 5/3. We report the
# normalized L1, L2, Linf error norms summed over all components.
#
# The discretization is dG Q1 on a uniform mesh with n_k = 24 elements per
# edge (2304 degrees of freedom per component). The rows of Table 1 are
# obtained by increasing "mesh refinement" from 0 to 5. For Q2 and Q3 set
# the "finite element ansatz" to "dG Q2" ("dG Q3") and the subdivisions to
# n_k = 16 (n_k = 12); the number of degrees of freedom then matches Q1.
# As in Section 5.2 of [1] also scale the entropy viscosity commutator
# with c_ev = 0.5 for Q2 and c_ev = 0.25 for Q3, i.e., set "evc factor" in
# subsection "F - HyperbolicModule/indicator" accordingly.
#
# The limiter bounds are relaxed with "relaxation factor = 4". With these
# settings Q2 and Q3 reproduce the convergence rates of Table 1 with L1
# errors 6-25% below the table (levels 0-3). For Q1 the errors agree
# within 11% on levels 0-2, but the rate stays at about 1.6 (Table 1:
# 1.8-1.9) and the error is 1.7 times larger on level 3. With the default
# relaxation factor 1 the Q3 rate drops to about 1.5.
#
# Table 5 of [1] (first-order method) is obtained by setting the limiter
# iterations to 0.
#
# [1] uses an "SSPRK-54" scheme which we replace by the explicit erk 54
# Runge-Kutta scheme. This is a reconstruction, small differences to the
# published numbers are expected.
#
# [1] M. Kronbichler, M. Maier, I. Tomas. Graph-based methods for
#     hyperbolic systems of conservation laws using discontinuous space
#     discretizations. Commun. Comput. Phys., 38:74-108, 2025.
#     arXiv:2402.04514
#
# [2] H. C. Yee, N. D. Sandham, M. J. Djomehri. Low-dissipative high-order
#     shock-capturing methods using characteristic-based filters. J.
#     Comput. Phys., 150(1):199-238, 1999.
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = isentropic_vortex

  set align time steps  = true

  set tasks             = error evaluation

  set final time        = 2.0
  set timer granularity = 2.0
end


subsection B - Equation
  set dimension = 2
  set equation  = euler
  set gamma     = 1.66666666666667
end


subsection C - Discretization
  set finite element ansatz = dG Q1

  set geometry              = rectangular domain
  set mesh refinement       = 0

  subsection rectangular domain
    set position bottom left      = -5, -5
    set position top right        =  5,  5
    set subdivisions x            = 24
    set subdivisions y            = 24

    set boundary condition bottom = dirichlet
    set boundary condition left   = dirichlet
    set boundary condition right  = dirichlet
    set boundary condition top    = dirichlet
  end
end


subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = isentropic vortex
  set direction     =  1,  1
  set position      = -1, -1

  subsection isentropic vortex
    set mach number = 1.41421356237310
    set beta        = 5
  end
end


subsection F - HyperbolicModule
  subsection limiter
    set iterations        = 2
    set relaxation factor = 4
  end
end


subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min               = 0.50
  set cfl max               = 0.50
  set cfl recovery strategy = none
  set time stepping scheme  = erk 54
end


subsection K - ErrorEvaluation
  set error normalize  = true
  set error quantities = rho, m_1, m_2, E
end
